oint final statement and even the draft  agenda was still under debate among eu  governments held up in large part it's  reported by the french but again the  fact the meeting is taking place at all  is an acknowledgment of the centrality  of the transatlantic relationship for  both the united states and for the  european union and there are many issues  they need to work on that will be  win-win for both sides and lose lose if  they don't take care of them so while  there's a lot of work to do as everyone  acknowledges there's a lot of work  that's already been done in just setting  up this trade and technology council 10  working groups already arranged so i  think that while everyone may not be on  the same page already today on day one  the very fact that they're all going to  be at the same table is definitely proof  that both sides want to move forward and  get past these disputes  terry shorts in brussels thank you very  much
 

